# armour/shared/pauldron_vented6_r: the legend VENTED pauldron on the right shoulder (vented.6; ARMOUR-X, wave 2: PLAN "The envelope in production", STYLE_P2 29).
# a flat-topped slab grown great, square at its corners, its face cut by dark vent slits between lit 2 px bands
# (the BROAD mass).
# 6 px past the 16 px shoulder line facing D (28 across with its pair; STYLE_P2 29.3). Side views wider and hanging lower.
# Rides the lean and the bob and lifts a pixel on wind-ups (`up`).
# Finish regions: R the slab's lip, P the lit bands, N the vents.
# Shared by the man and the woman (D10). Generated by ARMOUR-X genx.py from shapesx.py (re-run, never
# hand-edit the derived views). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
role pauldron vented.6
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys pauld
z 5
side R

# (ARMOUR fix2 r1, relic.py) the `metal-ember` views: hanging lames under the vented cop (D92: emberforged bulkier in the body)
